Supply and demand, supply and demand. Amulets of life saving are very
useful, with one, you cannot die. A demigod cannot die. So little
demand for the AoLs. On the other hand, a dilithium crystal is needed
for FTLT. FTLT is not a standard demigod ability, so there is a very
high demand for dilithium crystals.

And the reason that the AoLS is worth so little when you escape back
up the stairs, is that because of the high use of AoLs, they are mass-
produced outside of the dungeon. Probably under gruelling conditions
(If your employees die while making a AoLs it is not that much of a
problem if they die, you have a AoLs to revive them (and afterwards
send them back to work)). But they are so important that everybody has
a AoLs, just like mobile phones in our world. Only luddites have no
mobile phone (<-- flame bait ;) ). So they are of little value when
you bring them back up, because everybody has one (hey it is instant
healthcare, it solves hunger, war, everything. If we could make AoLs
they would be all over the place).

Of course that leaves the question, why didn't you take a whole stack
of AoLs into the dungeon? Well any adventurer who goes into a cave
that literally leads to hell. With less then a load of fully automatic
magic weapons and a army. Is either tricked into going in, or very
stupid. (I think generally adventurers are both).

(of course i'm not sure that you calculate AoLs score if you go up the
stairs).

